# The separator's own venv: what `mouth split` runs to make a song's stems and its
# instrumental. `mouth split --install` builds it under the separator home,
# ~/.local/share/ears/separator/venv, only when asked. It is never a dependency of the
# sessionvoice wheel: torch is about 1 GB, so it stays out of every pyproject.toml list.
# Compiled into requirements.lock, which is what install uses:
#   MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=14.0 uv pip compile requirements.in --python-version 3.12 \
#     --python-platform aarch64-apple-darwin --no-header --generate-hashes -o requirements.lock
# over the existing lock, so its pins hold (`--upgrade-package X` moves one; a fresh output
# file re-resolves and can drift them), then put the lock's header back. Install runs
# `uv pip install --require-hashes`, so the lock must carry a --hash for every pin. Every pin
# is a wheel: nothing is built, so no build backend is pinned.
# - demucs 4.1.0: the model code. 4.0.1 cannot load a local checkpoint on torch 2.6 or later
#   and needs torchaudio; 4.1.0 needs neither. Its `train` extra (torchaudio, dora-search)
#   is never installed.
# - torch: the speech venv's pin, so uv's cache can share it.
# - soundfile: writes the FLAC outputs (its wheel bundles libsndfile). run.py does the I/O
#   itself: no ffmpeg, no torchaudio, no demucs CLI.
demucs==4.1.0
torch==2.14.1
numpy
soundfile
